# The @bryanadamg scope lives on GitHub Packages, not npmjs. Only that scope is
# redirected — everything else still resolves from the default registry.
#
# No token here: npm expands ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} from the environment when it
# reads this file, so the file is safe to commit. Supply the value via:
#   - local dev  → export NODE_AUTH_TOKEN=... (it is in the repo-root .env)
#   - docker     → the `node_auth_token` build secret (see frontend/Dockerfile)
#   - CI/deploy  → forwarded from the NODE_AUTH_TOKEN GitHub secret
# If it is unset, npm sends the literal string and GitHub answers 401/404.
@bryanadamg:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
